  "caption": {
    "title_line": "🇯🇵 Going to Japan & have no idea what to do?",
    "body_draft": "comment \"JAPAN\" and i'll send you the full itinerary\n\nIf you're heading to Japan and have no idea where to start, here is the whole trip laid out so you can save it and stop stressing about the planning part.\n\nStart in Tokyo. Senso-ji is best before 8am while it's still empty and golden, Shibuya Crossing is worth crossing once, and teamLab Planets sells out weeks ahead so book it early. For food, the Lawson egg sando is an underrated konbini breakfast, and Omoide Yokocho in Shinjuku has tiny yakitori bars for about 150 to 300 yen a skewer. For shopping, Don Quijote and the Pokemon Center are the chaos everyone films, and Harajuku's Laforet plus the secondhand racks at RAGTAG cover the rest.\n\nFrom Tokyo, Kyoto is next. Arashiyama's bamboo grove, the Fushimi Inari torii gates, and the Kyoto Botanical Gardens are the three to prioritize.\n\nOsaka is close by and worth a couple of days. Dotonbori, Universal Studios, and Amerikamura are the main areas, and for shopping BIOTOP, Shinsaibashi PARCO, and the secondhand stores nearby are worth the detour.\n\nNara makes an easy day trip, mainly for the deer park, Todaiji, and the hike up Wakakusayama.\n\nHakone is the last stop, good for a night away from the cities, with its shrine, the volcanic valley at Owakudani, and a glass museum.\n\nSave this so you have the whole trip in one place, and follow for more Japan."
  },
